## User preferences

- When the user says "device hubがないです" with a screenshot -> match the installed Xcode UI, not an older menu name. [Task 1]

## Reusable knowledge

- For Xcode 26.6, use `Xcode > Open Developer Tool > Device Hub` or run-destination `Manage Devices…`; sequence Apple Account → Personal Team/automatic signing → `+ > Pair Nearby Device…` → Vision Pro `設定 > 一般 > リモートデバイス` PIN → Developer Mode/restart → Run. Same Wi-Fi and IPv6 are required; this device was unpaired and Team unset. [Task 1]
- Stage Sketch version 3 is the production source of truth; Vision Pro reads a derived `StageDocument schemaVersion 2` JSON through iCloud Drive/file selection. Never directly co-edit the web and Swift representations. Convert coordinates as `x=(0.5-u)*widthMeters`, `z=(0.5-v)*depthMeters`, `y=0`, `yawDegrees=facing`; lock four corner/direction tests. `sceneAnimMs` is UI speed, not rehearsal timing. [Task 2]
- Handoff: `show-creative-ideas/shosai-app/docs/VISION_PRO_REHEARSAL_EXTENSION_HANDOFF.md`. `npm test` passed 6/6 and StageCore passed 24/24 using `/tmp` cache/scratch paths; converter and physical/device/audio integration remain unimplemented. [Task 2]

## Failures and how to do differently

- CoreDevice/CoreSimulator and cache errors make CLI device state unreliable; check GUI Device Hub plus headset settings first. Do not call an unsigned build, docs, or test success a physical validation. [Task 1][Task 2]
- When Swift cache paths are denied, set `SWIFTPM_MODULECACHE_OVERRIDE` and `CLANG_MODULE_CACHE_PATH` plus `swift test --scratch-path /tmp/show-staging-stagecore-build`; keep proposed fields and unverified device/audio behavior explicitly separate. [Task 2]


